From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:47:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: set the RK806 reset mode on Orange Pi 5
 boards

The RK806 on the Orange Pi 5, 5B and 5 Pro has no rockchip,reset-mode,
so the driver leaves the RST_FUN field of SYS_CFG3 at whatever the PMIC
OTP or the boot firmware left there. It selects how the PMIC reacts to
a reset request on RESETB or on a PWRCTRL pin configured as reset:

  0 (RK806_RESTART)       power-cycle the PMIC and all its rails
  1 (RK806_RESET)         reset the "power off reset" registers and go
                          to ACTIVE; rails stay up, the SoC is not reset
  2 (RK806_RESET_NOTIFY)  as 1, and pull RESETB low for 5 ms

On a running Orange Pi 5, SYS_CFG3 reads 0x02, i.e. mode 0. Make that
explicit instead of relying on the firmware (mainline U-Boot's rk8xx
driver reads the same property and programs mode 2 when it is absent):
mode 0 is the only one that returns the whole board, including the
PMU1 (always-on) domain of the SoC, to its power-on state when the PMIC
is asked to reset. It is also what other RK806 boards that care about
a full reset use (Jaguar, Tiger). The vendor kernel programs mode 1 from
a generic Rockchip include shared by all its single-RK806 boards, but
mode 1 only resets the PMIC registers, so a hung SoC is not recovered.

Note that neither a reboot nor a watchdog timeout requests a PMIC reset
on these boards: PSCI SYSTEM_RESET and the watchdog use the CRU global
reset, the PWRCTRL pins are configured as "pin_fun0" (no function) and
the TSADC uses CRU mode for its over-temperature reset. This property
only fixes the behaviour for the cases where the PMIC is reset.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi
index fd0efa8d1..352e0552f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/leds/common.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/pinctrl/rockchip.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/soc/rockchip,vop2.h>
+#include "rk8xx.h"
 #include "rk3588s.dtsi"
 
 / {
@@ -334,6 +335,7 @@ rk806: pmic@0 {
 				<&rk806_dvs2_null>, <&rk806_dvs3_null>;
 		spi-max-frequency = <1000000>;
 		system-power-controller;
+		rockchip,reset-mode = <RK806_RESTART>;
 
 		vcc1-supply = <&vcc5v0_sys>;
 		vcc2-supply = <&vcc5v0_sys>;
